    "body": "I think it's within the range of possible correct designs we could settle on. It's not clear to me how the bookkeeping would work for things like Step 5.iv in your algorithm, because the synchronous processing and the navigation resolution step are in different processes.\r\n\r\nI think Chrome could probably get most of the way there if we could get rid of TaskE in my description and have TaskB not do a \"pending\" step and just immediately update the current step.  I don't know whether that would cause unacceptable race conditions, though.",
